In photography, especially in sports, people on the sidelines (or in the background) often appear blurry because they are either moving or the camera was not able to keep them in sharp focus due to the fast action on the field. This blur can be caused by motion blur — when the subject moves while the shutter is open — or by shallow depth of field, where only the main subjects are in focus.

Option A is incorrect because "blurry" doesn’t necessarily mean poor image quality; it’s a common effect in dynamic scenes.  
Option B and C are unrelated to the context of the photo.

So, **D** is the most accurate explanation.

✅ Final Answer: **D. They are in motion**
